## Runtime Architecture

{% if project_type == "script" %}
Current architecture: Python CLI package. The executable module lives under
`src/{{ python_package }}/`, tests live under `tests/`, and `make run` executes
the package module.
{% elif project_type == "library" %}
Current architecture: Python library package. Public imports are exported from
`src/{{ python_package }}/__init__.py`, `py.typed` marks the package as typed,
and build artifacts are written to `dist/`.
{% elif project_type == "backend" %}
Current architecture: FastAPI service. The app entry point is
`backend/src/app/main.py`; feature code is organized under `backend/src/app/modules/`.
The generated service exposes `/health`, `/ready`, and `/openapi.json`.
{% elif project_type == "frontend" %}
Current architecture: Nuxt application. Pages live under `frontend/pages/`,
feature code lives under `frontend/features/`, and shared frontend utilities
belong under `frontend/shared/` when introduced by a task.
{% elif project_type == "fullstack" %}
Current architecture: FastAPI backend and Nuxt frontend. The backend exports
OpenAPI with `make api-schema`; the frontend client is generated with
`make api-generate` and checked with `make api-check`.
{% if runtime_level == "production" %}
The production profile also generates local OCI image and Compose verification
targets for the backend and frontend runtime artifacts.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Quick Start

```bash
make setup
make check
make build
```

Run the generated project:

```bash
make run
```

{% if project_type == "fullstack" %}
Keep the API contract synchronized:

```bash
make api-check
```
{% endif %}

{% if project_type == "fullstack" and runtime_level == "production" %}
Verify production-like local artifacts:

```bash
make image-build
make image-inspect
make prod-up
make prod-status
make prod-smoke
make prod-down
```
{% endif %}

## Workflow

Use one active task at a time:

```bash
make agent-status
make agent-context TASK=<id>
make task-start TASK=<id>
make task-review TASK=<id>
make validate-project
make validate-docs
```

A1 and A2 approvals are human gates. Agents may prepare work and move it to
review, but must not approve it.

